Options:
1. BUC-test and try on all the stuff dropped by the watch, the priest,
random monsters and shop inventory; you are quite likely to be able to
pick up a couple of points worth of enchanted stuff.
2. If there was a bookstore, or even a general store, you may be
sitting on an unidentified scroll of enchant armor; IDing it will be a
bit more difficult without shopkeepers, though. If you have a magic
marker, lucky wizards have an *excellent* chance of being able to
write an unknown scroll; saccing will make you lucky (see #3).
3. With no priest, there's nothing stopping you from converting the
alter and sacfesting your heart out; get the luckstone first if
possible (see the praying spoiler for details on how to get protection
from saccing: http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html).
4. Keep going down the main dungeon; there's a reasonable chance of a
temple after DL9. If not, you may still find positively enchanted or
magic armor to boost your AC.

